# Build context exclusions.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE THE IMAGE IS UNBUILDABLE IN PRACTICE. `docker build` sends
# the whole directory to the daemon before running a single instruction, and
# after scripts/fetch_feeds.py has run, feeds/ holds several gigabytes of GTFS
# archives. The Dockerfile does not COPY any of it — the container fetches its
# own — but the context is assembled regardless, so the build appears to hang
# for minutes on "sending build context" and then copies data it will not use.

# Study working directory: downloaded archives, unpacked and normalised feeds.
# The container fetches these itself; the lock file is the only part worth
# carrying, and even that is not needed to build.
feeds/
data-ridership/

# Local build trees and generated results.
build/
build_*/
cmake-build-*/
results/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Compiled LaTeX and other generated documents.
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.aux
docs/*.log
docs/*.out
docs/*.toc
docs/*.synctex.gz
docs/*.fls
docs/*.fdb_latexmk

# Legacy data directories from the pre-study workflow.
data/
data_*/
raw_*/
*.zip

# Local-only working notes. These are git-ignored too; keeping them out of the
# image as well means a published container cannot leak them.
ANALYSIS.md
WORKFLOW.md
RESUME_PROMPT.md
BIBLE-*.md
WHERE-TO-GO-NEXT.md
